***REMOVED*** ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
***REMOVED*** Copy this file to `cloud-credentials.yaml`, fill in your S3 credentials, and
***REMOVED*** apply it manually. It is git-ignored (see .gitignore) and is NOT managed by
***REMOVED*** ArgoCD — this matches how the proxmox-csi-plugin Secret is handled.
***REMOVED***
***REMOVED***   cp cloud-credentials.yaml.example cloud-credentials.yaml
***REMOVED***   $EDITOR cloud-credentials.yaml
***REMOVED***   kubectl apply -f cloud-credentials.yaml
***REMOVED***
***REMOVED*** The key MUST be named `cloud` and the value is an AWS-style credentials file
***REMOVED*** (the Velero `aws` provider reads it via the standard AWS shared-credentials
***REMOVED*** format). Create the velero namespace first (or `--namespace=velero` won't bind).
***REMOVED*** ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: cloud-credentials
  namespace: velero
type: Opaque
stringData:
  cloud: |
    [default]
    aws_access_key_id = REPLACE_WITH_ACCESS_KEY
    aws_secret_access_key = REPLACE_WITH_SECRET_KEY
